  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_80522e7987f4493f85ef5717e28e2d32",
      "statement": "One image serves the web process, ingest work and one-off admin commands, with the vsir binary as the entrypoint — so the web service is a subcommand whose boot self-check runs before anything binds, and a misconfigured stack fails to start rather than serving.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a5e4cb89a4bd11547dc800e93ec1d8fdc5ad9f08d2e5a334f6125519c373658:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L64-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e4f1aa38e7c2b1835d158d04c0d1e84ac6396d115760145752136149effe0db:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.test.yml#L41-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a5762ad849e7d30f99577e5757736b587166f38aa45124725a9366691a64b96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15731a0be8e547329630ee0880045df1",
      "statement": "The image base is pinned by digest rather than tag, dependencies are installed from a hash-pinned lock file with --require-hashes so a substituted artefact fails the build, and the build stage's virtualenv is copied forward so no build tooling survives into the runtime layer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L13-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12aa647619202c240850f393c4c93bfd0b03d7f07d620733b80b088d46e9bee7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8aa28e84402e40d49ef7ab34ca38a888",
      "statement": "The runtime image runs as a non-root uid with no login shell and carries no configuration or secret, which is what makes running it with a read-only root filesystem and a writable tmpfs viable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L37-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f649978aa9529d6208a920c2471a0b664f4d1c6b74998ebd87d55ad5f2f397c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L66-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15dea45820f6aaad1cd404a6bf5e8667b4237cdcda4554f3619ed2c4954c2fd2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2878d2df5a4d4faebf03d6db5e67df21",
      "statement": "The document store's mount point is created and chowned in the image itself, because Docker initialises a fresh named volume from whatever is at the mount point — ownership included — so with nothing there the directory is root-owned and the container cannot write to its own volume; it is the one writable path outside tmpfs a read-only root allows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/Dockerfile#L54-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:815fe2bfb0cb987d25d225f0a06f1c604e881ecb80a575bf71097e3c8ce99d8c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_47d7d2ca9dbd4cd3b2be899d549b125c",
      "statement": "The console image pins its base by digest, installs from the lockfile so a mismatch fails the build, and serves with the framework's preview server rather than a static file server — because the API proxy is declared on the preview server too, keeping the container same-origin with the service.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/Dockerfile#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a0cf506876b82fc4cc0fd5602da6fd9e07cac8a5e9e474af23e43e905f53c4f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4993bbdaad6448eaaa0f6bc42fd2a9f0",
      "statement": "The dev stack publishes deliberately unusual loopback-bound ports — the store on 6353 and the API on 8055 — because the machine already runs a store on the conventional ports, and a stack that quietly answered from the wrong instance is worse than one that will not start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L11-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4362014e197c214eb9d701f60fd9acca01a044f2576106f7d110188ecded1994:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L136-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39200877b9a8fbe27a9fea7490f6cc11d6c50c029cdf9397ecf6165dc0e71770:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L29-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f3652b21f5606cea7c6fc70347f0945acd3d6f670f0068d969f60740d78f158:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_39eff22e9d2f4a28811b9c5f6e46b200",
      "statement": "A one-off init service creates the collection before the server can boot, because the server refuses a payload schema that does not match the index schema and \"does not exist\" does not match — and it is an admin process of the same image rather than a branch inside the server.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L46-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76b9551d833ccb500a3d6415d834c653dce8062ab073aa5f620a46b56c74e3ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f07f5898dd8e4608b1ca8467d27b49a5",
      "statement": "The dev stack mounts the corpus and fixtures read-only — nothing in the pipeline writes there because exports stream from the index — and mounts the document store writable as a host directory rather than a named volume, so ingested PDFs are visible where the operator works instead of inside a Docker VM.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L103-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be00e5056f02d9f578f68d240dfee76201f6c063953a1c4e7dbd31f0f5b85498:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a49d64fe6b7471a82f7227eb4e0ef8e",
      "statement": "The VLM credential is absent from the image and from the compose file, interpolated from the environment and read only under the live backend.",
      "evidence": [
