    {
      "id": "claim_3559d3aa50654e9990a0133c44be5fa7",
      "statement": "The test store is published on 6335 and never 6334, because 6334 is the dev instance's gRPC port and colliding with it would let a test run read and wipe dev data; the store version is pinned identically across dev, test and production because a differing store is a correctness difference.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.test.yml#L20-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd909f5e60d9a96e59384f77b7dcc1f180a3d1246c72f4c404ae5e73143581e7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8124547be8914ebdaa4d2a6956287d1d",
      "statement": "The test stack reads its bearer token from a test-specific variable rather than the production one, because compose interpolates from the developer's own environment file and the suites assert about the credential the container was handed — while the dev stack deliberately reads the same variable the CLI and a direct server run read, so one machine has one token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.test.yml#L41-L48",
