    {
      "id": "claim_ca22c8d42c60484bb115697c74627959",
      "statement": "The stack script wraps the dev stack with up, status, seed, logs, an arbitrary vsir subcommand in the stack's own image, and down with an optional wipe — resolving the running container's token lazily because before the stack is up there is no container to ask, and reading JSON with a small Python helper rather than requiring a JSON CLI tool.",
